    84	  new cells use the same configurations as the D2+H3 records they are paired with (the recorded 1-ulp deviation stays as
    85	  it is).
    86	- **Pairing and code checks (draft 5).** Before any episode the driver refuses a job whose runner, salt, configuration,
    87	  root, seeds, rule parameters, or context differ from its frozen reference's provenance; an unknown commit; a runner or
    88	  `sim/` that differs from protocol-v2; an output inside `--src` or `eval/all`; and a salt mismatch. The inventory records
    89	  Python, numpy, machine, platform, and the driver's hash.
    90	- **Validation before spend (free, on the Mac).** (a) Reproduction of the registered `headline@rho0.2|F111|D2` search and
    91	  evaluation. Draft 4 required identical knobs and per-seed gains. Measured on 2026-11-09/10: a Mac arm64 run and a Linux
    92	  amd64 container run both match on configuration, salt, runner, budget, rule parameters, episode count (15,660), archive
    93	  sizes, and the twin result, with selected knobs equal to 2.6e-13 relative and per-seed gains to 2.0e-14; evaluating the
    94	  registered knobs on the Mac gives per-seed gains within 5e-17 of the record (102 of 200 seeds bit-identical). Last-bit
    95	  arithmetic differences grow through the search; these runs did not reproduce bit identity across platforms, and the
    96	  draft-4 rule is replaced as a recorded deviation. **Draft-5 criterion** (`compare()`). Exact: the provenance keys runner, salt, configuration, rule
    97	  parameters, root, training, validation and evaluation seeds, context and budget (the commit may differ); the episode
    98	  count; the attack and twin archive sizes; `best_source`; the discrete knobs; the search and evaluation dependency ids;
    99	  the reference hash. Every value finite. Tolerance: continuous knobs within 1e-9 relative and per-seed
   100	  gains within 1e-9 absolute (about 10^4 times the drift measured, and far below the paired standard error of about
   101	  0.0009). The Mac runs pass this criterion. **Pod gate:** the pod first reruns the same reproduction (about 0.34 USD of
   102	  billed time: 2,084 s search plus evaluation at 0.56 USD per hour); the 18 cells start only if it passes the draft-5
   103	  criterion; a bit-identical result on the pod is reported as such. The reproduction path runs every pre-episode check
   104	  (salt, commit, code, pairing, configuration) before its search and saves `gate.json` and an inventory with the
   105	  environment (Python, numpy with BLAS and LAPACK, SciPy, CMA, CPU). (b) An
   106	  integration test runs the complete path (input copies, search, pre-evaluation freeze, evaluation, doubling, inventory)
   107	  for one fresh-market cell at smoke size, including the driver's acceptance check, which proves every dependency
   108	  resolves (passed, 2026-11-09). (d) Doubling ground truth: the driver's doubling stage reruns the registered doubling
   109	  check of `fresh0@rho0.2|F111|D2+H3|profit` on the Mac (`--reproduce-doubling`), compared by `compare_doubling()`:
   110	  exact on the flag, the seeds and the discrete knobs; 1e-9 on the continuous held-out knobs, the attack and reference
   111	  changes, and the held-out per-seed gains. The saved result must pass before any pod is created. (c) Unit tests: the driver refuses a
   112	  changed reference hash, a missing input record, a wrong configuration hash, and an output directory inside `eval/all`.
   113	
   114	## 4. Diagnostics (evaluation only, no search)
   115	
   116	For three rules on seven markets: the base and doubled D2+H3 winners (42 policies) and the base D2 winners (21; the doubled
   117	D2 winners are not included), on the 200 evaluation seeds, re-run with reset and ban instrumentation (63 single-policy
   118	evaluations; the existing gain records carry no reset counts, so none is reused); the selected `x`; per episode the number of resets, the probability of at least one reset, the rounds of resets,
   119	and the rounds spent banned. Check that every D2 winner has zero resets. **Reverse switch (draft 5):** each of the 18 D2 winners re-evaluated with
   120	`x = 1` and every other knob unchanged (18 more evaluations). The diagnostics are built and tested in the driver (`diagnostics`
   121	stage) before any pod. Order: the instrumentation is validated on the registered headline cells before the pod; the
   122	diagnostics of the 18 new D2 winners and their reverse switches run on the Mac after the pod's records are retrieved.
   123	Construction: a D2 winner is embedded in D2+H3 by adding `x` (0 for itself, 1 for the reverse switch); each switch is
   124	the mean difference of normalised profits on the evaluation seeds, the reference cancelling. Resets are the focal
   125	provider's identities of generation 1 or more; ban rounds are the ban lengths imposed on its identities; rounds without
   126	an offer are counted separately. Spot check: `fresh0@rho0.2|F111` is also evaluated on the pod, and the Mac values must
   127	meet the draft-5 tolerance against it. **Fixed-policy switch:** each of the 42 D2+H3
   128	winners re-evaluated with `x` set to 0 and every other knob unchanged (42 more; a winner that already has `x = 0` is
   129	reported as identical and not re-run); g(winner) - g(winner, x = 0) is the effect of the switch
   130	without re-optimisation, reported beside I.
   131	
   132	## 5. Analysis (fixed now)
   133	
   134	- **Intervals.** Per market: paired seed bootstrap (9,999 resamples, percentile, 95%), the same resampled seed indices for
   135	  every rule and family of that market, so contrasts across rules stay paired. Pooled: equal market weights; in each
   136	  replicate, seeds are resampled independently within each market and the pooled statistic is the mean of the six market
   137	  means; percentile interval. Nominal and descriptive; conditional on the six markets and the frozen policies and
   138	  references.
   139	- **Statistics.** I(r, m) and pooled I(r); the contrasts I(B3) - I(R3) and I(C*) - I(R3); the absolute gaps
   140	  G(D2+H3) = g_B3 - g_R3 under D2+H3 and G(D2) under D2, pooled.
   141	- **Share.** S = 1 - pooled G(D2) / pooled G(D2+H3), a ratio of pooled contrasts, computed in every bootstrap replicate.
   142	  S is reported only if the lower bound of pooled G(D2+H3) exceeds 0.05; otherwise "not defined". No clipping; S can be
   143	  negative or above 1. The absolute gaps are always reported beside it.
   144	- **Market sensitivity (draft 5).** The sign count of I(B3) - I(R3) and I(C*) - I(R3) over the six markets, and S with
   145	  each market left out in turn (six values), each with its own five-market denominator gate (lower bound of the
   146	  five-market pooled G(D2+H3) above 0.05; otherwise that value is "not defined"), for the base and the doubled results
   147	  separately. A nested best-of sensitivity (the better of the D2 and D2+H3 winners per cell) is deferred: it is not
   148	  part of this plan.
   149	- **Doubling flags.** For each D2 cell, the attack change and the reference-reselection change of its doubling check are
   150	  reported separately.
   151	- **Doubled versions** of the same statistics, as in the paper's `tab:ph-doubled`. The base (frozen) searches are primary,
   152	  as in the paper; the doubled versions are reported beside them.
   153	- No confirmatory test, no multiplicity family, no change to any registered decision.
   154	
   155	## 6. Pre-specified expectations and labels
   156	
   157	Written before any fresh D2 result exists. **The six markets, their seeds, and their D2+H3 outcomes were already observed;
   158	only the D2 outcomes are unseen.** This is a descriptive follow-up specified on 2026-11-09 after the round-9 review and
   159	after the headline contrast was seen, not an independent replication.
   160	
   161	Expectations: on all six fresh markets (each market counted; a single market against it fails the expectation), I(B3) > I(R3) and I(C*) > I(R3); pooled S defined and greater than 0.5. Expectations are
   162	scored on point estimates (this is a descriptive follow-up; "met" does not mean that an interval excludes the threshold),
   163	with the denominator gate of section 5 applied separately to the base and the doubled results. Each expectation is
   164	scored as met, failed, or not established: **met** if it holds under both the base and the doubled searches; **failed** if
   165	it fails under both; **not established (search-sensitive)** if the two disagree. An undefined S and a missing cell are
